WrapModule
├── constructor
│   ├── when wrappedNative is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with WrapModule_ZeroWrappedNative
│   ├── when wrappedNative has no code
│   │   └── it should revert with WrapModule_WrappedNativeNotContract
│   └── when wrappedNative is a contract
│       └── it should set wrappedNative
├── executeNative
│   ├── when amount is zero
│   │   └── it should revert with WrapModule_ValueMismatch
│   ├── when value differs from amount
│   │   └── it should revert with WrapModule_ValueMismatch
│   ├── when the wrapper credits less than the deposit
│   │   └── it should revert with WrapModule_WrapAmountMismatch
│   ├── when the wrapper credits one to one
│   │   ├── it should return success with amountOut equal to amount
│   │   ├── it should return wrappedNative as outputToken
│   │   ├── it should transfer the wrapped balance to the caller
│   │   ├── it should hold no native and no wrapped balance afterwards
│   │   └── it should emit Wrapped
│   └── fuzz
│       └── when any non-zero value is wrapped
│           └── it should credit the caller exactly that amount
├── execute
│   └── it should return a failed result with "Native input only"
├── validate
│   ├── when token is not the native sentinel
│   │   └── it should return false with "Native input only"
│   ├── when amount is zero
│   │   └── it should return false with "Zero amount"
│   ├── when caller native balance is insufficient
│   │   └── it should return false with "Insufficient balance"
│   └── when all checks pass
│       └── it should return true with empty reason
├── estimateOutput
│   ├── it should return amount as estimatedOutput
│   └── it should return wrappedNative as outputToken
└── moduleType
    ├── it should return "WRAP"
    └── it should report native input support
